   "text": "I read the structure in five parts and assembled them into one SMILES.\n\n**Fragments**\n- **Left end:** a benzhydryl amide (NH\u2013CHPh\u2082) on an L\u2011glutamine residue, whose side chain is CH\u2082CH\u2082C(=O)NH\u2082.\n- **Bicyclic core:** a pyrrolidine fused to an eight\u2011membered diazocine ring. The ring nitrogen carries the linker acyl group. The carbon next to the ring carbonyl carries an NH\u2013C(=O) amide to the indole.\n- **Indole:** a 2\u2011carboxamide bearing a CF\u2082\u2013P(=O)(OH)\u2082 group at C5.\n- **Linker:** C(=O)\u2013(CH\u2082)\u2086\u2013C(=O)NH. I counted seven bonds between the two carbonyl carbons, which gives six CH\u2082 groups; the zigzag spacing was slightly irregular, so the count of six is the least certain part of the reading.\n- **Right end:** a VHL\u2011type ligand. It has a tert\u2011leucine (tBu) unit, a 4\u2011hydroxyproline, and an NH\u2013CH(CH\u2083)\u2013aryl group leading to a 4\u2011methylthiazol\u20115\u2011yl ring.\n\n**Stereochemistry**\n- Glutamine \u03b1\u2011carbon: S, from the hashed bond to the side\u2011chain CH\u2082.\n- Pyrrolidine \u03b1\u2011carbon of the bicycle: S, from the hashed bond to the carbonyl.\n- Ring\u2011fusion carbon: R, from the hashed bond to the diazocine CH\u2082.\n- Diazocine carbon bearing the indole amide: S, from the hashed bond to NH.\n- Benzylic carbon: S, from the hashed methyl.\n- tert\u2011Leucine and hydroxyproline: I took these as the standard VH032 configuration, (2S,4R) for the hydroxyproline, rather than deriving them from the wedges.\n\nI derived each tag from the wedge/hash geometry and CIP priorities, then checked the tert\u2011leucine and hydroxyproline tags against the known VH032 SMILES.\n\nSMILES: NC(=O)CC[C@H](NC(=O)[C@@H]1CC[C@@H]2CCN(C(=O)CCCCCCC(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)(C)C)C(=O)N3C[C@H](O)C[C@H]3C(=O)N[C@@H](C)c3ccc(cc3)-c3scnc3C)C[C@H](NC(=O)c3cc4cc(C(F)(F)P(=O)(O)O)ccc4[nH]3)C(=O)N12)C(=O)NC(c1ccccc1)c1ccccc1"
